BE-300 2.4.18: disable CF/IDE in the default NAND profile.

The mega-patch turned on CONFIG_CASIO_BE300_CF + CONFIG_IDE for the
opt-in CF recovery boot. Without `--cf <image>` attached, the emulator's
IDE decode at 0x170 returns garbage status (0x50 with a junk model
name) and the 2.4 IDE driver enters an infinite `hda: lost interrupt`
loop during partition probe. That hangs init *before* NAND, touchscreen,
and Stowaway keyboard register — i.e. before VFS mounts root — so the
default boot stalls.

Disable CONFIG_IDE in the default config_be300. CF is re-enabled by
the future configs/be300_2_4_cf.config overlay (Phase 7 of the plan)
which a separate build_be300_2_4_cf_image.sh will merge before
configuring.

This is the minimum change to unblock the rest of the HW-parity work.
The CF IDE driver itself (cf_be300.c) and the IRQ cascade
(CASIO_BE300_IRQ_CASCADE=y) stay in the tree.

--- a/config_be300
+++ b/config_be300
@@ -136,12 +136,18 @@
 CONFIG_CASIO_BE300_NAND=y
 CONFIG_CASIO_BE300_TOUCH=y
 CONFIG_CASIO_BE300_STOWAWAY=y
-CONFIG_CASIO_BE300_CF=y
+# CF/IDE host is opt-in via configs/be300_2_4_cf.config — the 2.4 IDE
+# driver issues SET_GEOMETRY / INITIALIZE_DEVICE_PARAMETERS during probe,
+# which the emulator's CF model doesn't implement, so without --cf
+# attached `hda` finds garbage status and spins forever in `lost
+# interrupt`, blocking NAND/touch/keyboard init. Keep off in the default
+# NAND profile; reenable when building the CF recovery image.
+# CONFIG_CASIO_BE300_CF is not set
 CONFIG_CASIO_BE300_IRQ_CASCADE=y
-CONFIG_IDE=y
-CONFIG_BLK_DEV_IDE=y
-CONFIG_BLK_DEV_IDEDISK=y
-CONFIG_IDEDISK_MULTI_MODE=y
+# CONFIG_IDE is not set
+# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_IDE is not set
+# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_IDEDISK is not set
+# CONFIG_IDEDISK_MULTI_MODE is not set
 
 #
 # Parallel port support
